From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Navras98 <andrea.sforna@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mitigate tapjacking for file picker

Instant selection right after the picker opens (e.g. via an overlay-driven
tap) uploads the file with no chance to cancel (Vanadium #1116). Require
the picker to be visible for a minimum dwell time before accepting the
result, as suggested in the issue (delay like permission dialogues).
---
 ui/android/java/src/org/chromium/ui/base/SelectFileDialog.java | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/android/java/src/org/chromium/ui/base/SelectFileDialog.java b/ui/android/java/src/org/chromium/ui/base/SelectFileDialog.java
--- a/ui/android/java/src/org/chromium/ui/base/SelectFileDialog.java
+++ b/ui/android/java/src/org/chromium/ui/base/SelectFileDialog.java
@@ -258,2 +258,6 @@
 
+    // Vanadium #1116 anti-tapjacking: ignore picker results arriving suspiciously
+    // fast after showing it; an overlay-driven tap could otherwise select+upload instantly.
+    private static final long MIN_PICKER_VISIBLE_TIME_MS = 1500;
+    private long mPickerShownTimeMs;
     private long mNativeSelectFileDialog;
@@ -348,2 +348,3 @@
             WindowAndroid window) {
+        mPickerShownTimeMs = System.currentTimeMillis();
         mIntentAction = intentAction;
@@ -967,2 +967,6 @@
     public void onIntentCompleted(int resultCode, @Nullable Intent results) {
+        if (System.currentTimeMillis() - mPickerShownTimeMs < MIN_PICKER_VISIBLE_TIME_MS) {
+            onFileNotSelected();
+            return;
+        }
         if (sPhotoPicker != null) {
